The flight model -- x1_skyracer.xml, the files it assembles, Engines/, Systems/, Controls.xml, Sensors.xml, Visual.xml
and firmwares/ -- is PteroLabs' work, distributed under the GNU General Public License v3.0; see LICENSE in this folder
for its text. Its numbers come from:

  The designer's X1 SkyRacer flight model kit (X1_SkyRacer_PteroSim.zip, October 2026) and the concept model it is
  generated from: the geometry, rotor positions and spins, sensor mounts, tanks, wheels, 1.13 duct gain and 600 lbf
  pusher thrust.

  The designer's data for this model (2026-10-21): the mass list and its 7.895 % reduction to race weight, the
  generator's 1500 hp continuous and 2000 hp burst, and how the generator lags demand while the accumulator covers it.

  X1 Racing Rule Book v1.0: the 3,500 lb take-off weight, 500 lb of ballast, 200 lb of propane, the 10 kWh accumulator
  limit, the duct sizes and the fan layout.

  AVL 3.52, Drela and Youngren: the stability derivatives in Aero.xml, from a vortex-lattice model of the concept
  model's wings, body and pusher shrouds.

  Hoerner, Fluid-Dynamic Drag and Fluid-Dynamic Lift; Raymer, Aircraft Design; NACA TN 3038: the stall, the flat plate
  past it, and the drag build-up.

  Abbott and von Doenhoff, Theory of Wing Sections: the NACA 4409 polars behind the fan tables.

  EMRAX 268 and 348 data sheets: the drives' current limit, as a ratio of peak to continuous torque.

Chosen, with no source, and marked so where they appear: the 800 V bus, the motor losses, the fan blades and the motors
sized for them, the stall angles, the interference drag, the generator's time constant, the accumulator's taper and the
wheels' spring and damper. README.md lists the model's known limits.

The meshes (meshes/) are built from the flight model kit's generator scripts, with X1 Racing's livery, and are not
under the GPL: the design's published sources state no licence of their own, and the geometry, the livery and the X1
name remain their owners'. They are used here by the designer's permission. Changes made here: the body was generated at
a higher resolution, unwrapped and baked to base colour and ORM textures; a cockpit opening with seats was cut under
the canopy; the pushers moved out to y +-0.705 m, where their 26 in bores clear the tail boom; the fan blades and hubs
are PteroLabs' redesign.
